# {{ project_name }}

Infrastructure managed by [Bay](https://github.com/AltanS/bay).

## Setup

```bash
# Install framework
make bay:setup

# Create vault password
echo 'your-vault-password' > .vault_pass
```

## Configuration

Edit these files before your first deploy:

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `hosts/production` | Server IP address(es) |
| `group_vars/all/services.yml` | Service and accessory definitions |
| `group_vars/all/users.yml` | SSH keys for server access |
| `group_vars/production/domains.yml` | Domain name and SSL email |
| `group_vars/production/secrets.yml` | Encrypted credentials |

## DNS Setup
{% if not multi_region %}

Create a wildcard DNS A record pointing to your server:

```
*.{{ domain_base }} → {{ server_ip }}
```

This allows Traefik to route traffic for all service subdomains (e.g., `status.{{ domain_base }}`) to your server.
{% else %}

Each region needs its own wildcard DNS A record:

| Region | DNS Record | Server IP |
|--------|-----------|-----------|
{% for region in regions %}
| {{ region.name }} | `*.{{ region.name }}.{{ domain_base }}` | {{ region.server_ip }} |
{% endfor %}

Bay's multi-region mode uses per-region subdomain prefixes (e.g., `status.eu.{{ domain_base }}`).
{% if regions|length == 1 %}

When you add more regions, create additional wildcard A records:
`*.newregion.{{ domain_base }} → <new-region-ip>`
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Deploy

```bash
# First time — provision and harden the server
bin/bay provision production

# Deploy services (auto-detects if infrastructure rig is needed)
bin/bay deploy production

# Force full deploy including infrastructure roles
bin/bay deploy --rig production

# Dry run (preview changes)
bin/bay deploy production -- --check --diff
```

